1
00:00:03,382 --> 00:00:10,912
Create and submit a claim — Billing ▸ Claims — Build a claim from a visit, code it, and send it to the clearinghouse.

2
00:00:16,151 --> 00:00:21,097
Billing ▸ Claims is the money pipeline: every claim and where it has got to.

3
00:00:21,097 --> 00:00:31,544
Status is the whole story — draft not sent, submitted waiting, paid settled, denied needs work.

4
00:00:31,544 --> 00:00:40,164
Pick the patient and the claim inherits their insurance — no re-keying policy numbers.

5
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:46,127
Service date and charge come from the visit you are billing for.

6
00:00:46,127 --> 00:00:59,517
Diagnosis codes are searched, not remembered — type the code or the words and pick from the list.

7
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:13,112
The procedure code is what you are billing; the diagnosis is why. Payers check that the two agree.

8
00:01:13,112 --> 00:01:22,161
Created as a draft. Nothing has been sent yet — drafts are safe to fix.

9
00:01:22,161 --> 00:01:27,201
Submit EDI 837 sends it to the clearinghouse in the format payers expect.

10
00:01:27,201 --> 00:01:32,873
From here it comes back paid, or denied with a reason — and a denial goes straight to the Denials queue.

11
00:01:33,377 --> 00:01:47,297
What you just did

12
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:53,580
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
